  "notes": "{縮|ちぢ}める is a transitive verb ({他動詞|たどうし}) meaning to make something shorter or smaller.\n\nINTRANSITIVE PAIR: {縮|ちぢ}む (to shrink)\n- {縮|ちぢ}む (intransitive): The sweater shrinks.\n- {縮|ちぢ}める (transitive): I shorten the time.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{縮|ちぢ}めている indicates the action of shortening is ongoing.\n\nPARTICLE PATTERNS:\n- [thing]を{縮|ちぢ}める — to shorten/shrink [thing]\n- [distance/gap]を{縮|ちぢ}める — to close [distance/gap]\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {時間|じかん}を{縮|ちぢ}める (shorten time)\n- {距離|きょり}を{縮|ちぢ}める (close the distance)\n- {差|さ}を{縮|ちぢ}める (narrow the gap)\n- {身|み}を{縮|ちぢ}める (shrink back, cringe)\n\nFIGURATIVE USE:\n{距離|きょり}を{縮|ちぢ}める can mean to become closer emotionally or to catch up in a competition.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {短|みじか}くする: to make short (more neutral)\n- {縮小|しゅくしょう}する: to reduce, scale down (formal)",
